 INPUT CARD>! C2H7O3Cl | RHF/UHF instability check -- NO-MIX CONTROL                        
 INPUT CARD>! Same geometry/basis as caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPP-uhfcheck.inp, but WITHOUT    
 INPUT CARD>! $GUESS MIX=.TRUE. Purpose: the MIX run converged to -491.6953591779 with      
 INPUT CARD>! S-SQUARED=1.487, ~15 kcal/mol below the RHF energy (-491.6712565) -- but      
 INPUT CARD>! MIX aggressively rotates HOMO/LUMO before the first cycle, which can land     
 INPUT CARD>! UHF on a genuinely different, disconnected SCF solution rather than proving   
 INPUT CARD>! the RHF/closed-shell ground state itself is unstable. This control checks     
 INPUT CARD>! that: if plain UHF (normal HUCKEL guess, no forced symmetry breaking) also    
 INPUT CARD>! drifts to the same low-S-SQUARED-contaminated solution, that is much          
 INPUT CARD>! stronger evidence of a real instability. If it converges back to              
 INPUT CARD>! ~-491.67 with S-SQUARED~=0, the closed-shell solution is a perfectly good     
 INPUT CARD>! stable UHF solution too, and the MIX result is a separate accessible state    
 INPUT CARD>! rather than proof the RHF ground state is unstable.                           
 INPUT CARD>                                                                                
 INPUT CARD> $CONTRL SCFTYP=UHF RUNTYP=ENERGY DFTTYP=wB97X-D                                
 INPUT CARD>         COORD=UNIQUE MULT=1 ICHARG=0 NOSYM=1 MAXIT=200                         
